-- Migration 59: triage status assignment — `manual_override` field + `status_change_log` table (Track Q.3)
--
-- Track Q's triage layer re-derives every affected entity's `status`
-- (`active` | `reference`) deterministically from the config `status_rules`
-- after each extraction. Two new schema objects make that safe and auditable:
--
-- 1. `manual_override` on `entity` — a dedicated bool COLUMN (operator decision
--    R2: column over a `properties` key). When true, the operator has pinned the
--    status by hand and AUTOMATION MUST NEVER OVERWRITE IT. A column is chosen
--    because it is queryable/indexable for the UI status filter and is immune to
--    the `properties` union-merge overwrite semantics in `EntityRepository`
--    (entity.py merges `properties` on upsert, which could silently clobber a
--    properties-key override). Default false so every pre-existing row reads back
--    as "automation-owned" without a data backfill.
--
-- 2. `status_change_log` — a queryable, restart-safe SurrealDB TABLE (operator
--    decision R3: table over an append-only file) recording every automation
--    status change with old/new/reason/batch provenance. One row per ACTUAL
--    change; an unchanged re-run writes nothing (idempotency lives in the
--    service, not the schema).
--
-- migration 39 already defines `entity.status` as a FREE `string` (DEFAULT
-- 'active', NO enum ASSERT), so introducing the new `"reference"` value needs NO
-- constraint change here. `idx_entity_status` (migration 39) already indexes it.
--
-- Additive + idempotent, following migration 54's precedent: every statement is
-- `IF NOT EXISTS`, never `OVERWRITE`, so re-applying on a DB that already carries
-- these objects is a no-op and nothing predating Q.3 (status, its index) is
-- touched. The B.0 testcontainers roundtrip harness validates the replay.

DEFINE FIELD IF NOT EXISTS manual_override ON entity TYPE bool DEFAULT false;

DEFINE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS status_change_log SCHEMAFULL;

DEFINE FIELD IF NOT EXISTS entity ON status_change_log TYPE record<entity>;
DEFINE FIELD IF NOT EXISTS old_status ON status_change_log TYPE string;
DEFINE FIELD IF NOT EXISTS new_status ON status_change_log TYPE string;
DEFINE FIELD IF NOT EXISTS reason ON status_change_log TYPE string;
DEFINE FIELD IF NOT EXISTS batch_id ON status_change_log TYPE string;
DEFINE FIELD IF NOT EXISTS changed_at ON status_change_log TYPE datetime DEFAULT time::now();

DEFINE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_status_change_log_entity ON status_change_log FIELDS entity;
DEFINE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_status_change_log_batch ON status_change_log FIELDS batch_id;
